  "title": "VISIT: T+7 Keep Exploring",
  "subject": "The rest of T.R.'s story, from home",
  "preheader": "Six chapters of his life, quizzes for every level and a podcast recorded at the Library.",
  "fromName": "Theodore Roosevelt Presidential Library",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "props": {
        "src": "proposals/img/visit-t-plus-7-keep-exploring-header.jpg",
        "alt": "Theodore Roosevelt Presidential Library",
        "href": "https://www.trlibrary.com"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "text": "The Story Keeps Going",
        "align": "center"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "props": {
        "html": "Hello [[FIRSTNAME OR \"Friend\"]],<br><br>Thank you for visiting the Theodore Roosevelt Presidential Library. The galleries cover a lot of ground in one visit. The rest of Theodore Roosevelt's life is online, told in six chapters, from a Manhattan childhood to an unmapped river in the Amazon.",
        "align": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "columns",
      "props": {
        "cols": [
          {
            "src": "proposals/img/pv-tr-badlands.jpg",
            "alt": "Theodore Roosevelt in buckskin standing guard with his rifle",
            "heading": "The Badlands",
            "text": "He came to Dakota to hunt a bison and stayed to run cattle on the Little Missouri. Read how the Badlands gave him a new life.",
            "label": "Read the Chapter",
            "href": "https://www.trlibrary.com/tr/badlands"
          },
          {
            "src": "proposals/img/pv-tr-conservation.jpg",
            "alt": "Yosemite Valley with El Capitan and Half Dome",
            "heading": "Conservation",
            "text": "Parks, forests, monuments and bird reserves: roughly 230 million acres protected, and how he did it.",
            "label": "Explore",
            "href": "https://www.trlibrary.com/tr/presidency/conservation"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "button",
      "props": {
        "label": "Explore T.R.'s Life",
        "href": "https://www.trlibrary.com/tr"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "divider",
      "props": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "text": "Put Your Knowledge to Work",
        "align": "center"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "columns",
      "props": {
        "cols": [
          {
            "src": "proposals/img/pv-quiz-myths.jpg",
            "alt": "Clifford Berryman 1902 cartoon Drawing the Line in Mississippi",
            "heading": "Fact or Fiction",
            "text": "Fifteen questions separating the famous stories from the record.",
            "label": "Take the Quiz",
            "href": "https://www.trlibrary.com/quiz/myths"
          },
          {
            "src": "proposals/img/pv-quiz-family.jpg",
            "alt": "A grassy coulee opening onto badlands country",
            "heading": "What Lives Out There",
            "text": "Fifteen questions on the wildlife T.R. watched from the saddle, what was lost and what you can see today.",
            "label": "Take the Quiz",
            "href": "https://www.trlibrary.com/quiz/badlands-wildlife"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "props": {
        "html": "Dozens more, from family editions to expert level, at <a href=\"https://www.trlibrary.com/quiz\">trlibrary.com/quiz</a>.",
        "align": "center"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "divider",
      "props": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "text": "For the Teacher in Your Life",
        "align": "center"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "props": {
        "html": "Teach with TR is the Library's collection of classroom resources for K-12: lesson plans built on North Dakota and national standards, primary-source packets on the Rough Riders, the Pure Food and Drug Act, women's suffrage and more, timelines (one written just for kids), and hands-on activities, from designing a cattle brand to making T.R.'s own frying pan bread.",
        "align": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "button",
      "props": {
        "label": "Explore Teach with TR",
        "href": "https://www.trlibrary.com/teach-tr"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "props": {
        "html": "<b>Know a teacher who would use these?</b> Forward this email, or send them <a href=\"https://www.trlibrary.com/teach-tr\">trlibrary.com/teach-tr</a>.",
        "align": "center"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "divider",
      "props": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "text": "Watch and Tune In Live",
        "align": "center"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "props": {
        "html": "Book talks with authors, curator talks from the collection and Taste of History stream live on the Library's YouTube channel at 5:30 p.m. MT. Subscribe, like the videos you enjoy and turn on notifications to be the first to know when the next virtual event goes live.",
        "align": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "columns",
      "props": {
        "cols": [
          {
            "src": "proposals/img/pv-watch-youtube.jpg",
            "alt": "Book Talk title card for a virtual program streamed by the Library",
            "heading": "Live on YouTube",
            "text": "Virtual events stream on the Library channel. Subscribe so the next one lands in your feed.",
            "label": "Subscribe",
            "href": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCPOPdzgpO4liPSWkk7VqS5A?sub_confirmation=1"
          },
          {
            "src": "proposals/img/pv-watch-videos.jpg",
            "alt": "Curator Talk title card from the Library video collection",
            "heading": "The Video Library",
            "text": "Every past talk, film and program, sorted into series, at trlibrary.com/video.",
            "label": "Start Watching",
            "href": "https://www.trlibrary.com/video"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "divider",
      "props": {}
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "text": "Listen: Good Citizen",
        "align": "center"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "props": {
        "html": "Ted Roosevelt V hosts conversations with people who step into the arena to build up the country and protect the planet. The <i>Live from the TRPL</i> series is recorded at the Library, beginning with presidential historian Doris Kearns Goodwin. Good Citizen was a 2024 Webby Award Honoree.",
        "align": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "props": {
        "html": "<a href=\"https://podcasts.apple.com/us/podcast/good-citizen/id1713230937\">Apple Podcasts</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/show/7ywQA9wJGztUPmedmG6BSe\">Spotify</a> &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL-sck-PjBiFcxu6QSF_0u7aDB9EJ5mLe_\">YouTube</a>",
        "align": "center"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "button",
      "props": {
        "label": "Listen to Good Citizen",
        "href": "https://www.trlibrary.com/podcast/good-citizen"
      }
    },
